        <history>
          <p>Brigg Fair takes its theme from an English folk song collected by Percy Grainger in Lincolnshire, which Grainger passed to Delius with enthusiasm. Delius transformed the simple tune into an extended orchestral rhapsody of shifting harmonic colour, and the work is widely regarded as the piece that established his mature orchestral voice to English audiences.</p>
